WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.650
Armenia had taken Christianity
as its faith

2
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:06.754
early in the fourth century.

3
00:00:07.114 --> 00:00:12.244
In 449 Yazdegerd II,
shahanshah of Sasanian Persia,

4
00:00:12.284 --> 00:00:15.564
commanded the Armenians
to renounce Christianity

5
00:00:15.604 --> 00:00:17.584
for Zoroastrianism.

6
00:00:17.944 --> 00:00:20.892
In 450 much of Armenia rose.

7
00:00:20.932 --> 00:00:24.662
At the head of the rising
stood Vardan Mamikonian,

8
00:00:24.702 --> 00:00:28.797
sparapet, the hereditary commander
of Armenia's army.

9
00:00:29.157 --> 00:00:31.827
In 451 the Persian army came,

10
00:00:31.867 --> 00:00:35.519
with its elite cavalry
and a corps of war elephants.

11
00:00:35.559 --> 00:00:38.529
Vardan drew up his army
on the plain of Avarayr,

12
00:00:38.569 --> 00:00:40.593
by the river Tghmut.

13
00:00:40.953 --> 00:00:43.321
The Armenians won the first clashes.

14
00:00:43.361 --> 00:00:46.371
Then the Persian reserves
surrounded Vardan's men,

15
00:00:46.411 --> 00:00:48.211
and Vardan fell there.

16
00:00:48.444 --> 00:00:51.534
The field was lost,
yet the faith held:

17
00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:55.294
in 484 his nephew Vahan
won freedom of worship

18
00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.483
by the Treaty of Nvarsak.

19
00:00:57.843 --> 00:01:01.134
Stand where Vardan stood.

